		<meta property="schema:abstract">The Belief of Catholics is an account of the grounds of Catholic belief and of the Catholic system as it is held and lived, written for the general reader.</meta>
		<dc:description>
			&lt;p&gt;The Belief of Catholics is an account of the grounds of Catholic belief and of the Catholic system as it is held and lived, written for the general reader. Knox wrote it in 1927 for the “What I Believe” series, in which writers of differing convictions each stated their own. It has a preface and nineteen chapters, of which the first is so far transcribed here.&lt;/p&gt;
		</dc:description>
